<title>USA: Fountain says it will get cash for shares.</title>
<headline>Fountain says it will get cash for shares.</headline>
<dateline>LARGO, Fla. 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fountain Pharmaceuticals Inc said Tuesday it signed a letter of intent with private investment firm Eaglestone Capital Services Inc of Long Beach, Calif., to exchange preferred shares for an undisclosed amount of cash.</p>
<p>&quot;Our company has needed money for some time to take the technology forward,&quot; said John Walsh, Fountain's chief executive. The company is developing encapsulated delivery systems for the pharmaceutical and cosmetic industries.</p>
</text>
